issue_comments:
Section 3.5.7.2 of the JSR-283 specification (aka, "JCR 2.0") states:
{quote}
A mixin node type may have one or more supertypes, which must also be mixin types.
{quote}

At the moment however, ModeShape does not perform any kind of validation in this regard, allowing a mixin type to inherit from a non-mixin type. 
We should add this validation so that an error is raised during type registration if the above case occurs.

When property has been removed from node and then changes must be saved to external source they are not available in connector's updateDocument(delta) method.

class org.modeshape.jcr.cache.document.SessionNode.java has following code which returns change list for removed properties:
{code}
        public Set<Name> removedPropertyNames() {
            Set<Name> result = new HashSet<Name>();
            result.addAll(changedProperties().keySet());
            return result;
        }
{code}
instead of 
{code}
result.addAll(changedProperties().keySet()) 
{code}
